        },
        "response": {
          "bodySize": 23994,
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "size": 23994,
            "text": "{\"records\":[{\"sha\":\"ba329e2351c6c670655c69e33c8279ad76ad0368\",\"parents\":[\"ffd288f6acbbf770f107b8f4598d0a38a851a056\",\"6424eec24733ba61890dcd41353a0e8e9c4f78a2\"],\"message\":\"Merge walk-change\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian Bright\",\"email\":\"julian@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-10-24T18:50:10Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Introspection\",\"email\":\"noreply@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-10-24T18:50:10Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"ffd288f6acbbf770f107b8f4598d0a38a851a056\",\"parents\":[\"1c7bdac3ab0eb3f4f02ac7832746bf996cc1de3d\",\"c88ba41e2ab1ea7c58f7ad8918d8b9470e3b5e59\"],\"message\":\"Merge walk-change\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian Bright\",\"email\":\"julian@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-10-24T18:35:30Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Introspection\",\"email\":\"noreply@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-10-24T18:35:30Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"1c7bdac3ab0eb3f4f02ac7832746bf996cc1de3d\",\"parents\":[\"4666130ef73f2ae0a607cf5450a0f7a1ac1e716b\",\"801247e312053f5dea3471c6682f1fffce64d65c\"],\"message\":\"Merge walk-change\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian Bright\",\"email\":\"julian@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-10-24T18:28:03Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Introspection\",\"email\":\"noreply@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-10-24T18:28:03Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"4666130ef73f2ae0a607cf5450a0f7a1ac1e716b\",\"parents\":[\"7f1b30bdc28cab38088de86becab9a69280b1bda\"],\"message\":\"feat: a write-granting manifest for the SDK walk's GitHub lane (#16)\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-10-23T22:55:44Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-10-23T22:55:44Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"7f1b30bdc28cab38088de86becab9a69280b1bda\",\"parents\":[\"4c9cca91890806e4d231d039448629a459cbf172\"],\"message\":\"fix(scripted): pin the platform-served introspection/scripted-llm double (#14)\\n\\nProblem: the scripted agent pins a borrowed OpenRouter catalog id the AI gateway\\ndiverts, so each pi release that drops the id breaks every scripted run.\\nObjective: the scripted agent must pin introspection/scripted-llm, the model the\\nruntime declares through its own introspection provider and whose host reaches\\nonly the gateway's scripted-llm route, so no third-party catalog sits on the path.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019zJo9h4ppTXcyJJpXU9hrJ\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"yoga@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-10-20T04:56:56Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-10-20T04:56:56Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"4c9cca91890806e4d231d039448629a459cbf172\",\"parents\":[\"0cd1553b818dfddc630f1335ab75f2fc56916cdb\"],\"message\":\"chore: run the smoke's real-model agents on claude-haiku-5-5 (#15)\\n\\nProblem: the smoke's real-model agents ran on claude-sonnet-4-6, about 19 times the per-call cost of claude-haiku-5-5 for the same tokens.\\nObjective: every real-model smoke agent must run on claude-haiku-5-5; the scripted agent stays on its free double.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SzLsV86GDXxbuikHHJEcdK\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"yoga@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-10-20T03:35:26Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-10-20T03:35:26Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"0cd1553b818dfddc630f1335ab75f2fc56916cdb\",\"parents\":[\"97ea6bcaaf41c95d5b23943dba380c99641b399e\"],\"message\":\"feat(mcp): add the connector-bound MCP variant the smoke's mcp_connector stage launches (#12)\\n\\n* feat(mcp): add the connector-bound MCP variant the smoke's mcp_connector stage launches\\n\\nNo smoke stage makes a working MCP call, so a break between a connector and\\nthe MCP server it reaches ships unseen: a binding the platform drops is demoted\\nto optional and the agent answers anyway. The new mcp/ variant declares a\\nrequired hello-mcp server that allows only echo, and its manifest names the\\nhello-mcp connector the runtime needs. The smoke binds that connector to the\\npublic MCP example server and checks the server's echo comes back as the\\nagent's tool result.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SzLsV86GDXxbuikHHJEcdK\\n\\n* docs(mcp): say the manifest's connector declaration reaches only a discovered runtime\\n\\nThe smoke creates the mcp variant's runtime through the API, so the\\nmanifest's runtime.connectors does not reach it, and the stage's readiness\\nread comes from the server the recipe declares.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SzLsV86GDXxbuikHHJEcdK\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"yoga@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-10-16T01:13:35Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-10-16T01:13:35Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"97ea6bcaaf41c95d5b23943dba380c99641b399e\",\"parents\":[\"b2adb66907dddf873e8891ed3b6784898051817e\"],\"message\":\"fix(scripted): pin the reserved scripted-double id the gateway now diverts (#11)\\n\\nOpenRouter retired openai/gpt-oss-20b:free, so pi no longer lists it and the\\nscripted agent fails at sandbox startup with Unknown Pi model. The AI gateway\\nnow reserves openrouter/google/gemma-4-31b-it:free for the scripted-llm double\\n(introspection-org/introspection-cloud#3175), so the scripted agent pins that id.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CohZp5xtrEUEitbdJhtAun\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"yoga@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T12:07:29Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T12:07:29Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"b2adb66907dddf873e8891ed3b6784898051817e\",\"parents\":[\"34aef0483e5dd0471c23b968070980c521a0db48\"],\"message\":\"fix: migrate off the unpublished pi-recipes package (#10)\\n\\n* fix: migrate off the unpublished pi-recipes package\\n\\n`@introspection-ai/pi-recipes` was renamed to `@introspection-ai/recipes`\\nand the old name was unpublished from npm, so every sandbox boot that\\nmaterializes this recipe dies resolving it:\\n\\n  ERR_PNPM_FETCH_404 GET .../@introspection-ai%2Fpi-recipes: Not Found\\n\\n`--prod` does not save us. With no lockfile, pnpm resolves the full\\nmanifest — devDependencies included — before pruning to prod, so a dead\\ndevDependency fails the install outright. Reproduced against the\\nruntime's exact command, then verified fixed.\\n\\nThe rename carried two changes beyond the name:\\n\\n  - The new package intentionally ships no `recipes` executable (\\\"The\\n    package intentionally has no `recipes` executable\\\" — its README).\\n    `introspection check` is the supported validator, so the check\\n    scripts move to the CLI. `--profile` has no successor and is dropped.\\n  - The action repo was renamed too: pi-recipes-action -> recipes-action.\\n    GitHub redirects, so this is cosmetic here, but the action is\\n    independently broken — its v0 tag predates the rename and still\\n    npx-es the 404 package. That fix belongs in recipes-action.\\n\\nBoth hostile variants keep their contracts: crash/ resolves and then\\ndies with its intended hostile_boot message rather than being masked by\\na registry 404, and unbound/ installs clean. All 3 recipes validate.\\n\\n* ci: retrigger checks against recipes-action v0.2.0\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T20:27:40Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-08-26T20:27:40Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"34aef0483e5dd0471c23b968070980c521a0db48\",\"parents\":[\"77f30a565951c36a096ee6453c683d7184fb7c0b\"],\"message\":\"chore(manifest): drop the legacy slug field so discovery parses again (#9)\\n\\nThe control plane rejects `slug` (and `runtime_name`, `runtime.name`) as an\\nunsupported Runtime identity field: the Runtime Group identity is the manifest\\nfilename, `.introspection/<slug>.yaml`. All three manifests still declared it, so\\npush-discovery of this repo fails validation before any manifest is read.\\n\\nRemoving the field leaves the filename as the sole identity, which resolves to the\\nsame group slugs the probes already pin (smoke-test-agent, smoke-test-agent-crash,\\nsmoke-test-agent-unbound), so nothing downstream changes name.\\n\\nVerified by parsing all three through the control plane's own\\nparse_recipe_manifest plus validate_manifest_set: each yields its expected\\ngroup_slug and path, and re-adding `slug` still fails validation.\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"yoga@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-07-28T01:49:19Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-07-28T01:49:19Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"77f30a565951c36a096ee6453c683d7184fb7c0b\",\"parents\":[\"993917997c07d1c3236d30b6bd91ac9cef14a010\"],\"message\":\"fix(scripted): pin the reserved OpenRouter id the gateway diverts (#8)\\n\\nThe scripted agent pinned `scripted/deterministic/v1`, an id that no longer\\nresolves. The runtime's synthetic-model branch that understood a `scripted/`\\nprefix is gone, and the gateway rule that matched the prefix is now an exact\\nmatch on a real catalog id, so model resolution fails at sandbox startup with\\n`Unknown Pi model` and the sandbox answers 503 on /ready for its whole life. A\\ncapacity run against this agent reports created N and ready 0.\\n\\n`openrouter/openai/gpt-oss-20b:free` is a real pi catalog entry, so the runtime\\nresolves it with no special casing, and the AI gateway diverts that exact id to\\nthe in-cluster scripted-llm double where the divert is enabled. Cost stays zero\\neither way: diverted, the double answers and the control plane prices the id at\\nzero; not diverted, OpenRouter's free tier answers and reports zero cost.\\n\\nVerified against the recipe-check binary vendored in @introspection-ai/recipes\\n0.14.1 (valid), and against the pi catalog the runtime loads: the new id is\\npresent as openai-completions at zero cost, the previous one is absent.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G6KFEH1ZnCsGgGGLhHzju8\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"yoga@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-07-27T07:46:53Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-07-27T07:46:53Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"993917997c07d1c3236d30b6bd91ac9cef14a010\",\"parents\":[\"8229c7004aee90bd8dab042b84325e004da0a741\"],\"message\":\"fix(unbound): nest agent MCP server selections under mcp.servers (#7)\\n\\nThe recipes package moved an agent's MCP server selections from a flat map\\nkeyed by server id to a `servers` map nested under `mcp`, and made that key\\nrequired. The unbound variant still carried the flat shape, so the checker\\nrejected it with two diagnostics:\\n\\n  [agent.mcp_servers_invalid] Agent mcp.servers is required\\n  [agent.mcp_key_unknown]     Unknown Agent mcp field 'dead-mcp'\\n\\nRecipe validation runs on task create, so every task against this recipe\\nreturned 409 and the staging smoke went red on the binding_wedge stage for\\nevery deployment leg.\\n\\nThe package manifest at unbound/package.json already declares its MCP servers\\nunder the nested shape, so this puts the agent definition on the same contract.\\n\\nVerified with the recipe-check binary vendored in @introspection-ai/recipes\\n0.14.1 through its own checkRecipeAtLoad entry point: the flat shape reproduces\\nboth diagnostics above, the nested shape returns valid, and the root and crash\\nvariants stay valid.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G6KFEH1ZnCsGgGGLhHzju8\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"yoga@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-07-27T04:40:27Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-07-27T04:40:27Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"8229c7004aee90bd8dab042b84325e004da0a741\",\"parents\":[\"2153450e0ad16ca2b85a42d158d0572edb9cd8cd\"],\"message\":\"fix: address the scripted double by its scripted/ model id (#6)\\n\\nThe runtime resolves a scripted model through the `scripted/` prefix and builds\\na synthetic openai-completions model for it. It carries no entry for the retired\\n`scripted-llm/default` id, so an agent pinning that id fails during startup with\\n`Unknown Pi model \\\"scripted-llm/default\\\"`, the session is never constructed, and\\nthe sandbox serves 503 on /ready until the caller's readiness budget expires.\\nA capacity run against this recipe therefore creates tasks that never reach\\nready and records zero turns.\\n\\nPin `scripted/deterministic/v1` so the gateway routes the request to the double\\nand the control plane prices it at $0. The sub-path names this harness because\\nthe double echoes whichever id it receives, so a vendor model name there would\\ndescribe a model that never runs.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G6KFEH1ZnCsGgGGLhHzju8\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"yoga@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-07-26T23:22:49Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-07-26T23:22:49Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"2153450e0ad16ca2b85a42d158d0572edb9cd8cd\",\"parents\":[\"817eaf102c5147c51522f4fcc705ffea602f326d\"],\"message\":\"feat: restore failure-contract variants — crash/ as before, unbound/ declaration-only (#5)\\n\\n* feat: restore failure-contract variants — crash/ as before, unbound/ declaration-only\\n\\ncrash/ returns unchanged from #3. unbound/ drops the .pi/mcp.local.json\\nbinding: hidden dirs are stripped at materialization (only\\n.introspection/*.yaml ships), so a committed binding never reached the\\ndeployed sandbox and the bound-but-unreachable design silently degraded\\nto required-but-missing. Declaring that shape directly is the honest\\ninjection; the probe's settle contract covers both the fatal\\nmaterialization path and any future demotion.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01218V6j8JmRECiQskaYWy8c\\n\\n* fix: gate crash/'s death on being the materialized recipe\\n\\nIsolation rehearsals (introspection-cloud smoke runs 1812/1818/1819)\\nproved the ungated postinstall fires during ROOT-recipe materialization\\nand kills any root launch at a sha containing crash/ — while sibling\\nmanifests and the declaration-only unbound/ are inert. The hook now\\nexits 0 when a ../package.json exists (nested sibling content) and\\nstill dies deterministically when crash/ is the workspace root (a\\nsub_path=crash launch), making the variants safe to merge to the\\ndefault branch.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01218V6j8JmRECiQskaYWy8c\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"yoga@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T10:05:38Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T10:05:38Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"817eaf102c5147c51522f4fcc705ffea602f326d\",\"parents\":[\"3d00ef7d41de0efdf66b2b1f78e7e31e7f27c1ed\"],\"message\":\"chore: bump VERSION to 0.0.2 (re-pin recipes after variant revert)\\n\\nStandard recipe bump: triggers recipe re-versioning so the standing\\nsmoke projects pick up a fresh root recipe pin at current HEAD, healing\\nthe staging smoke's bake stage (currently resolving a stale variant\\nrecipe row).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01218V6j8JmRECiQskaYWy8c\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"cyharyanto@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T05:35:19Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"cyharyanto@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T05:35:19Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"3d00ef7d41de0efdf66b2b1f78e7e31e7f27c1ed\",\"parents\":[\"01c375f432b6bc83d79967d95894bca5f0a78340\"],\"message\":\"Revert \\\"feat: hostile failure-contract variants (crash/, unbound/) (#3)\\\" (#4)\\n\\nThis reverts commit 01c375f432b6bc83d79967d95894bca5f0a78340.\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"yoga@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T05:02:43Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T05:02:43Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"01c375f432b6bc83d79967d95894bca5f0a78340\",\"parents\":[\"5384d120b6855e81236b236c6dfb6bf7520c382e\"],\"message\":\"feat: hostile failure-contract variants (crash/, unbound/) (#3)\\n\\nCompanion to introspection-cloud#1663 (failure-contract smoke stages).\\nTwo deliberately broken sibling recipes, each its own sub-path recipe\\nroot with a reconciling .introspection manifest:\\n\\n- crash/ — postinstall exits 1, so the sandbox dies at startup before\\n  the agent session becomes ready. Injects hostile_boot's startup-death\\n  row (legible failure, bake-claim release, retry admitted). Mirrors the\\n  real incident population: recipes with failing dependency setup.\\n- unbound/ — declares a required MCP server (pi.mcp.servers) that the\\n  agent opts into, bound via a committed .pi/mcp.local.json to an\\n  unreachable URL (127.0.0.1:9 — deterministic refusal, no secrets).\\n  Injects binding_wedge's dead-binding row: the task must settle (serve\\n  or fail legibly), never wedge in queued. A missing binding is\\n  deliberately non-fatal in the runtime, so bound-but-dead is the honest\\n  reproduction of the production wedge.\\n\\nTheir brokenness is the point; the READMEs say so to guard against\\nwell-meaning fixes.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01218V6j8JmRECiQskaYWy8c\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Christoforus Yoga Haryanto\",\"email\":\"yoga@introspection.dev\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T04:18:55Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-07-21T04:18:55Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"5384d120b6855e81236b236c6dfb6bf7520c382e\",\"parents\":[\"31ed0a8750dbca80a14f85bdc7c327f047efed73\"],\"message\":\"chore: adopt recipe conventions and the shared validation action (#2)\\n\\n- Add a recipe-validation workflow via introspection-org/pi-recipes-action@v0\\n  (runs on every push/PR) and a .githooks/pre-commit that runs the check.\\n- package.json: add check/check:json/prepare scripts and the\\n  @introspection-ai/pi-recipes devDependency, plus conventional\\n  keywords/license/peerDependencies. (No \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\" — src/ is CommonJS.)\\n- agents/agent.yaml: use model.thinking_level instead of reasoning_effort,\\n  clearing the thinkingLevel validation warning.\\n\\nRecipe now validates clean at the ci and publish profiles.\\n\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TA79t4EF7eTTSLPm5SJgXj\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"author\":{\"name\":\"Julian\",\"email\":\"brightsparc@gmail.com\",\"date\":\"2026-07-19T02:36:28Z\"},\"committer\":{\"name\":\"GitHub\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"date\":\"2026-07-19T02:36:28Z\"}},{\"sha\":\"31ed0a8750dbca80a14f85bdc7c327f047efed73\",\"parents\":[\"515ce315b962f239bad2e53ab67d62a0783efc2d\"],\"message\":\"probe bump 3a5fac8